    "['broadcast-suppression cir [parameter1] cbs [parameter2] inbound vlan [parameter3]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family ethernet-switching storm-control broadcast level 38400 burst-size 7200000', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Juniper equivalent command for the given Huawei broadcast suppression configuration:\\n\\n##\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family ethernet-switching storm-control broadcast level 38400 burst-size 7200000\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family ethernet-switching vlan members 10\\n##\\n\\nNotes:\\n1. Juniper uses \"storm-control\" instead of \"suppression\" terminology\\n2. The CIR (38400) becomes \"level\" in Juniper\\n3. CBS (7200000) becomes \"burst-size\" \\n4. Juniper requires explicit VLAN membership configuration\\n5. The command is applied at the interface level rather than specifying \"inbound vlan\" separately\\n6. For GE2/0/0, you would replace \"ge-1/0/0\" with \"ge-2/0/0\" in the command', 'trans_template': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family ethernet-switching storm-control broadcast level 38400 burst-size 7200000'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family ethernet-switching vlan members 10', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Juniper equivalent command for the given Huawei broadcast suppression configuration:\\n\\n##\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family ethernet-switching storm-control broadcast level 38400 burst-size 7200000\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 unit 0 family ethernet-switching vlan members 10\\n##\\n\\nNotes:\\n1. Juniper uses \"storm-control\" instead of \"suppression\" terminology\\n2. The CIR (38400) becomes \"level\" in Juniper\\n3. CBS (7200000) becomes \"burst-size\" \\n4. Juniper requires explicit VLA